## Customer Analysis — STAR Analysis

**Situation:**
The business has **44,524 customers**, an **AOV of ₹649**, **21% repeat customers**, and **37% loyalty members**. The customer base is predominantly **male (55%)**, while **Adults** represent the largest age group. Customer ratings average **4.1/5**. 

**Task:**
Increase **customer retention, repeat purchases, and customer lifetime value** by better utilizing customer segments and loyalty data.

**Action:**

* Increase the **21% repeat-customer rate** through personalized offers and loyalty rewards.
* Convert more of the **37% loyalty members** into frequent/repeat customers.
* Target promotions based on **age group, gender, city, and customer segment** rather than using a single offer for everyone.
* Focus on improving customer experience in key feedback areas such as **delivery, taste, packaging, and food quality**. 

**Result:**
The biggest opportunity is **customer retention rather than just acquisition**. Increasing repeat purchases and loyalty engagement can raise **customer lifetime value and AOV**, while addressing feedback issues can help strengthen overall customer satisfaction.
